{
  "date": "2026-10-11",
  "period_start": "2026-10-04",
  "period_end": "2026-10-10",
  "title": "Play became a media playground",
  "summary": "A week of new ways to make media, more models to choose from, and fewer steps between finding a capability and using it.\n\nPlay now brings image, video, and audio generation into one place, with uploads, previews, downloads, shareable settings, and API examples built from each request. Earlier changes stopped it from sending reference images to models that cannot use them, while the SDK added reference image, video, and audio options for supported video models. The interface and the API are getting closer to describing the same thing.\n\nFLUX.3 Image, Seedream 5.0 Flash, and Nano Banana 2.1 expanded image generation and editing. Grok Imagine Video 1.5 Lite joined video; Eleven v4, Eleven v4 Turbo, Qwen Audio 3.0 TTS Flash, and two MAI Voice models expanded speech. MAI Transcribe 2 added file and live transcription options. Output fixes also kept vertical video vertical and unseeded image requests random.\n\nLing 3.1 Flash, Nex N2.5 Pro and Mini, Mistral Large 4, Claude Haiku 5.5, and Step 5 Preview joined the text lineup. Liquid D1 and GPT-6 Luna Decisions added typed answers for structured questions, alongside an SDK decision helper. Every Chat text model gained a path through `/v1/responses`, and supported Claude and GPT models gained base64 PDF input. That is more choice without making every choice require a different API shape.\n\nModel-list APIs and MCP search gained query, capability, agent, and limit filters. Listings added tags, streaming support, and `paid_only` information; Enter gained a dated changelog for model and API changes. New discovery catalogs point agents toward hosted MCP servers, the API specification, and guides without requiring the URLs to be memorized first.",
  "pr_count": 231,
